"%lld sealed events in the last day against a habit of about %lld a day over the fortnight — %@× its own normal. Loud days have authors; the log knows them." = "%lld versigleti Ereignis im letschte Tag, gege e Gwohnheit vo öppe %lld pro Tag i de letschte vierzäh Täg — %@× vo sim eigene Normal. Luuti Täg händ Urheber; s Protokoll kennt si.";
"%lld shared days" = "%lld gmeinsami Täg";
", %lld of them placed in their rooms on the Map." = ", %lld devo i ihri Zimmer uf de Map gsetzt.";
", and the house was awake for much of it" = ", und s Huus isch für e grosse Teil devo wach gsi";
", on a night the house was awake after midnight" = ", i einere Nacht, wo s Huus nach Mitternacht wach gsi isch";
". A correlation, printed as one — not a cause." = ". E Korrelation, als eini druckt — kei Ursach.";
". Noted because tired operators and busy houses so often arrive together." = ". Vermerkt, wil müedi Operatorä und beschäftigti Hüüser so oft zäme aacho.";
"A new face on the wire" = "E neus Gsich am Draht";
"A regular — seen %lld times, roughly every %@ — has not been seen for %@. Silence from a regular is itself a signal: unplugged, moved, replaced, or gone." = "E Stammgascht — %lld Mal gseh, öppe all %@ — isch sit %@ nümme gseh worde. Stilli von e me Stammgascht isch sälber es Signal: usgsteckt, verschobe, ersetzt oder ewägg.";
